/* Shardwild overworld + Haven tiles: hand-drawn 8x8 art (Sprites). Generated by world_art.py + export_js.py in this folder.
 * NOTHING here is wired in. Rotmg adds it only after Joshua says go. game.js was not modified.
 *
 * FORMAT: rows + one hex palette per set, same as mkSprite; '.' = transparent.
 *   Opaque 8x8 tiles: ground.*[] variants, wall.wallTop/wallFace/wallDeep, hedge/post/vault pieces.
 *   Transparent 8x8 overlays: edges.* (terrain transitions), wall edge/corner/shadow pieces, details.*, lavaRims, carpetTrim.
 *   props.* are DECORATION SPRITES for mkSprite(rows,pal). Drawn WITHOUT outline because mkSprite adds the 1px #0d0b12
 *   outline itself, exactly as SPR.tree etc. are built today. Up to 8x8 (fountain 16x13, banners 6x8, bush 8x5).
 *
 * SETS
 *   WORLD_TILES.shore      zone 0 Saltmarsh Shore: ground.water/wet/sand, edges.wet (foam line over water) + edges.sand,
 *                          details (sand), waterDetails, props reed/drift/crate/boulder, wall = Gull Wreck ship planks.
 *   WORLD_TILES.greenmarch zone 1: ground.grass, edges.grass, details, props tree/bush/flower/stump/campfire/boulder, wall = mossy stone.
 *   WORLD_TILES.ashen      zone 2 Ashen Wilds: ground.ash + ground.lava (T_LAVA), edges.ash, lavaRims, props boulder/vent/ruin/stump,
 *                          wall = obsidian brick (Obsidian Ruin).
 *   WORLD_TILES.godlands   zone 3: ground.rock + ground.arena, edges.rock, edges.arena (gold curb), props pillar/statue/boulder/ruin/
 *                          brokenPillar (marble ruin used for T_RUIN in the Godlands and shore), wall = marble with gold band (Marble Temple).
 *   HAVEN_TILES            hub + vault: ground.meadow/path/pond/floor/carpet/rug/vaultFloor, edges.meadow/path/floorCurb/carpetTrim,
 *                          shadow pieces, details, wall.hedgeTop(2)/hedgeFace(2)/postTop/postFace/vaultTop/vaultFace, props
 *                          planter/bench/crate/pillar/tree/bush/flower/banner/bannerB/bannerG/torch/fountain.
 *
 * HOW GROUND FITS
 *   1. Each cell gets ONE terrain (tile id + zone; see wtClassify). Paint a ground variant: [0] ~55%, others share the rest (hash).
 *      Haven floor is 16x16 flagstones: ground.floor[set][quarter], set = hash(tx>>1,ty>>1), quarter = (tx&1)+2*(ty&1).
 *   2. TRANSITIONS: terrains have a priority  water/pond 0 < wet 1 < sand 2 < grass/meadow 3 < path 3.5 < ash 4 < rock 5 < arena 6 < floor 7.
 *      For every HIGHER-priority neighbour terrain B (lowest B first), paint B's edge overlay onto this cell:
 *        edges[B].n/s/w/e for each side whose neighbour is B (use the '2' variants, n2/s2/w2/e2, on ~50% of cells by hash),
 *        edges[B].nw/ne/sw/se when only the diagonal is B (neither adjacent side is B).
 *      All side pieces are 2px deep at their ends, so any mix of pieces lines up across tiles; corners join the sides.
 *      Result: wavy shorelines with a foam line, grass tufts spilling onto sand, ash creeping onto grass, stone edges onto ash, a gold
 *      curb around the arena, a stone curb where Haven floor meets the planting beds.
 *   3. Lava (T_LAVA): ground.lava + lavaRims n/s/w/e on sides not touching lava. Carpet/rug: carpetTrim on sides not touching carpet.
 *   4. DETAILS: ~5% of plain cells (3% meadow) get one details.* decal, only if the cell got no transition overlay and has no deco.
 *   5. WALL SHADOW: a non-wall cell directly below a wall gets wall.shadowN (that wall's set); directly right of a wall gets shadowW.
 *      Haven uses edges.shadowN/W on floor, edges.meadowShadowN/W on meadow, edges.vaultShadowN/W in the vault.
 *
 * HOW WALLS FIT (same cube scheme as the dungeons)
 *   Realm T_WALL uses WORLD_TILES[zone set].wall:
 *     south not wall -> wallFace (+edgeN if north not wall, +faceEdgeL/R if west/east not wall)
 *     all 8 neighbours wall -> wallDeep
 *     else wallTop + edgeN/edgeL/edgeR on open sides + cornerNW/NE/SW/SE notches (see wtLayers).
 *   Haven T_WALL: a LOW hedge. hedgeTop where the tile south is also wall, hedgeFace where it isn't (alternate '2' ~35%).
 *     Stone posts (postTop/postFace) ONLY at corners and ends: wallKind 2, or wallKind 1 when the wall isn't a straight run.
 *     Drop the old every-6th-tile post rhythm ((x+y*2)%6) so there is no big repeating wall pattern.
 *   Vault T_WALL: vaultTop / vaultFace with the realm edge pieces.
 *
 * WHAT IT REPLACES in game.js v25: GROUND table + groundRGB (T_WATER..T_ARENA and the T_WALL fallback), the T_LAVA branch in tileRGB,
 *   biomeWall, manorWall, stoneTop/stoneFront (vault walls), the T_WALL branches of wallRGB/wallLip and the Haven 1px wall lip in tileRGB,
 *   havenFloor, havenMeadow, havenPath, havenPond, vaultFloor, carpetRGB, rugRGB, and the SPR defs (lines ~186-221) for tree, boulder,
 *   fountain, reed, drift, flower, stump, vent, pillar, banner/bannerB/bannerG, bush, torch, planter, bench, crate, ruin, campfire, statue.
 *   Tile ids, TS=8, SOLID, DECO_SPR and world generation stay the same.
 *
 * INTEGRATION NOTES FOR ROTMG
 *   - SMOOTH BIOME BORDERS NEED ONE GENERATOR CHANGE: pickBand() currently flips a random coin per tile near each border, which
 *     makes the checkerboard speckle at every zone edge. pickBand_proposed.js (next to this file) swaps that for a smooth noise
 *     offset, so borders become wavy lines. It does not consume R(), so trees and spawns are unchanged, but structures can land in slightly
 *     different spots because they check zones. The 'after' previews use it. Without it the edge pieces still work but stay speckly.
 *   - Speed: wtLayers checks neighbours, so call it ONCE PER TILE in raster()/rasterVoid() and fill the 64 pixels from the layers.
 *     Don't call it per pixel through tileRGB. minimapRGB can just use the centre pixel of the layers.
 *   - Decorations: build SPR entries from props, e.g. SPR['w:'+set+':'+name]=mkSprite(rows,pal), and in raster() draw the one wtLayers
 *     returns in .deco (it picks the zone's version: shore/ash/godlands boulder, burnt ashen stump, etc.) at tx*TS-1,ty*TS-1 like today.
 *   - Haven dress: SPR.bush/banner/bannerB/bannerG/torch from HAVEN_TILES.props (same drawSpr call). Fountain: draw 1:1 at
 *     (fountain.x-9, fountain.y-8) with its own size (18x15 with outline) instead of the 20x20 scale.
 *   - Meadows off every edge: wtClassify returns meadow outside the Haven map. Draw a ring of outside cells (like drawDungeonVoid
 *     does for dungeons) with wtLayers + wtOutsideDeco(x,y) for scattered trees, instead of the flat #4e8a3c clear colour.
 *   - T_RUG has art (HAVEN_TILES.ground.rug + carpetTrim) but isn't placed anywhere in v25, so wtClassify doesn't map it.
 *   - Gates (drawGate), portals and labels are unchanged.
 */
